# AppVelocity — Cursor AI Rules
# This file gives Cursor deep context so every AI suggestion is on-brand.

## Project Identity
AppVelocity is a **monorepo** housing an AI-powered mobile development acceleration platform.
It contains 7 specialized agents, a shared infrastructure layer, a Next.js 14 web dashboard,
and a unified CLI. The active agent in development is **DesignToCodeAgent**.

## Monorepo Layout (pnpm workspaces)
```
packages/
  shared/core          → @appvelocity/shared-core   (AgentBase, types, logger)
  shared/langgraph     → @appvelocity/shared-langgraph (LangGraph workflow layer)
  shared/integrations  → @appvelocity/shared-integrations
  shared/ui            → @appvelocity/shared-ui
  shared/database      → @appvelocity/shared-database
  agents/design-to-code/core       → Figma API client, IR builder
  agents/design-to-code/workflow   → LangGraph planner/researcher/critic/generator
  agents/design-to-code/generators → React Native, Flutter code generators
  agents/access        → AccessAgent (planned)
  agents/shield        → ShieldAgent (planned)
  agents/perfect       → PerfectAgent (planned)
  agents/testiq        → TestIQAgent (planned)
  agents/devboost      → DevBoostAgent (planned)
  agents/compliance    → ComplianceAgent (planned)
  cli                  → @appvelocity/cli
  web                  → @appvelocity/web (Next.js 14, Tailwind, App Router)
```

## Critical Conventions
- **Language**: TypeScript 5.4+ strict mode everywhere. Never use `any` — use `unknown`.
- **Package manager**: pnpm 9. Use `workspace:*` for internal deps.
- **Build**: Turbo. Run `pnpm build` from root to build all; `pnpm dev` for watch mode.
- **Imports**: Use `@appvelocity/shared-core` not relative paths across packages.
- **Agent interface**: Every agent MUST extend `AgentBase` from `@appvelocity/shared-core`.
- **Tests**: Vitest. Co-locate test files as `*.test.ts` beside the source.
- **Commits**: Conventional commits — `feat(agent-name): ...`, `fix(web): ...`.

## Agent Contract (never deviate from this)
```typescript
abstract class AgentBase {
  abstract readonly name: string;
  abstract readonly version: string;
  abstract readonly description: string;
  abstract readonly capabilities: string[];
  abstract execute(input: AgentInput): Promise<AgentOutput>;
  abstract validate(input: AgentInput): ValidationResult;
  abstract estimateCost(input: AgentInput): CostEstimate;
  getHealth(): AgentHealth { ... }
}
```
- `AgentInput.action` is a string matching one of the agent's declared action IDs.
- `AgentOutput.success` must always be set, even on partial failures.
- Never throw from `execute()` — return `{ success: false, errors: [...] }`.

## Web App (packages/web)
- **Framework**: Next.js 14 App Router. Use Server Components by default.
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS. Use `av-card`, `av-badge`, `av-log` utility classes from globals.css.
- **State**: `useState` / `useReducer` for client components. SWR for data fetching.
- **Streaming**: Agent output uses Server-Sent Events. See `app/api/agents/stream/[jobId]/route.ts`.
- **Agent config**: All 7 agents are defined in `lib/agents.config.ts`. Never hard-code agent data elsewhere.
- **Agent registry**: `lib/agent-registry.ts` maps config → live instances. Wire new instances here.
- **API routes**:
  - `POST /api/agents/[agentId]` → launches a job, returns `{ jobId, streamUrl }`
  - `GET  /api/agents/status/[jobId]` → polls job status
  - `GET  /api/agents/stream/[jobId]` → SSE stream of logs/result

## DesignToCodeAgent Workflow (LangGraph)
```
START → planner → researcher → critic → [score<80: researcher loop] → generator → finalizer → END
```
- Planner uses strong model (gpt-4o / claude-3-5-sonnet).
- Researcher calls Figma REST API; rate-limited to 60 req/min; cached with LRU.
- Critic scores on: token coverage (>90%), naming, layout fidelity, completeness, code quality.
- Generator is staged: theme → atoms → molecules → organisms → screens → navigation → assets.
- All intermediate state is stored in `WorkflowState` typed object.

## Figma REST API (used by DesignToCodeAgent)
- Auth: `X-Figma-Token: {token}` header.
- File metadata: `GET /v1/files/:key`
- Variables / tokens: `GET /v1/files/:key/variables/local`
- Nodes: `GET /v1/files/:key/nodes?ids=comma,separated,ids`
- Image exports: `GET /v1/images/:key?ids=...&format=svg`
- Rate limit: ~60–100 req/min. Use `p-queue` with concurrency=5.

## Environment Variables
Defined in `.env.example` at repo root. Never commit `.env`.
- `FIGMA_ACCESS_TOKEN` — required for DesignToCodeAgent
- `OPENAI_API_KEY` or `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` — at least one required
- `LLM_PROVIDER` — `openai` or `anthropic`
- `REDIS_URL` — optional caching backend
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` — base URL for the web app (default: http://localhost:3000)

## Code Style
- Arrow functions for component callbacks.
- Named exports for components (`export function Foo` not `export default`).
- Default exports only for Next.js page/layout components.
- `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/intersections.
- Zod for all runtime validation at API boundaries.
- `async/await` — never raw `.then()` chains.

## What NOT to do
- Never import from `../../packages/...` across package boundaries — use workspace aliases.
- Never put agent business logic inside `packages/web`.
- Never call the Figma API directly from the web layer — always go through the agent.
- Never use `localStorage` or `sessionStorage` in server components.
- Never skip the Critic agent loop — it is a non-negotiable quality gate.

## Adding a New Agent (checklist)
1. Add entry to `packages/web/lib/agents.config.ts`
2. Create `packages/agents/<id>/` with `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `src/index.ts`
3. Implement `AgentBase` interface
4. Wire instance in `packages/web/lib/agent-registry.ts`
5. Update `pnpm-workspace.yaml` if the new package path isn't covered
6. Change `status` to `'active'` in `agents.config.ts`
